# Exam track — Theme: Summer — Sub-lesson 2: Key Phrases
# Plain @sentence blocks (no @question) — shorter restatements of the same
# interview facts that sub-lesson 3 answers in full.
#
# These are the learners' real answers, gathered by interview — do not "improve"
# or genericize them in a later editing pass. Two speakers share the theme, so
# some facts belong to one of them only (the December move vs the November move,
# the summer birthday vs the spring one); both are kept as they were said.
#
# LOD corrections applied: recommendéieren -> recommandéieren, Éisterräich ->
# Éisträich, besichen (to visit a person) -> besichtegen (to visit a place).
# Participle normalised to the corpus-dominant `kaaft` (16 uses) over `kaf` (1).

@lesson J1.02 "Summer Phrases"

